{title: Just Once More}
{subtitle: Judges 16:28–30; 13:5; 14:5–6; 15:15; 16:4–27}
{key: D#m}
{tempo: 63}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [D#m] | [D#m] | [D#m] | [B] |
| [C#] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D#m]Set apart to God before he ever saw the light
[B]No razor on his head and the [C#]Spirit gave him might
In the [D#m]vineyards of Timnah a young lion roared and ran
[B]And he tore the lion apart with [C#]his bare hands [D#m]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Down in the Valley of Sorek Delilah held him near
[B]The rulers of the Philistines [C#]put silver in her ear
Tell [D#m]me, where does your great strength come from
Night after night she pressed him till he [B]told her everything in his heart
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
She [C#]lulled him to sleep on her lap
[B]Seven braids fell to the [C#]floor
[B]Samson, the Philistines are upon [C#]you
But [B]he did not know that the LORD had left him
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D#m]They took his eyes and chained him, grinding [C#]grain in Gaza's jail
But [B]the hair of his head began to grow back
[C#]They brought him out to Dagon's house to laugh at what he'd [D#m]lost
Three thousand on the rooftop, and he [C#]stood between the posts
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[B]Sovereign LORD, remember me
[C#]Please, God, strengthen me just once more
Blind [D#m]and bound in the house of Dagon
[C#]Hands upon the pil[B]lars, I am crying out to you
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[C#]He pushed with all his [D#m]might [C#][B][C#][D#m][C#][B][C#]
[B]And the temple came down
[C#]He [B]pushed with all his might
And [C#]the [B]temple came down
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Sovereign LORD, [C#]re[B]member me
Please, God, strength[C#]en me [D#m]just once more
Blind and bound in [C#]the house of Dagon
[B]Hands upon the pillars, I am [C#]crying out to you [D#m][C#]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[B]Sovereign LORD, re[C#]member me
{end_of_verse}

